==Trivia==
*The word "''Skeleton''" comes from the Greek "''σκελετός''" (''skeletós''), meaning dried up or withered.
**The Giant Skeleton is 1 of 15 cards associated with [[Skeletons]], with the others being [[Bomber]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Tombstone]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Guards]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[Balloon]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Super Witch]], [[Graveyard]], [[Skeleton King]], and of course, Skeletons.
***In the Japanese language setting of the game, his description refers to how the Bomber is a tiny skeleton carrying a much smaller bomb.
***According to a Clash-A-Rama comic [https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/Clash-A-Rama!_Comic_Strips?file=BRING-YOUR-CHILD-TO-WORK-DAY_Final.jpg strip], a Skeleton is the Giant Skeleton's child.
*Bombs were first invented in China during the ninth century. Initially, they were made with ceramic material along with gunpowder, however, they were later changed to cast-iron shells with the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thunder_crash_bomb Thunder crash bomb] during the twelve century.
*The Giant Skeleton is 1 of 17 troops that inspired a troop in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Spear Goblins]], Bomber, [[Bats]], Skeleton Barrel, [[Minion Horde]], [[Firecracker]], [[Battle Ram]], [[Ice Golem]], [[Zappies]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], and [[Night Witch]].
**According to his [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Giant_Skeleton Clash of Clans counterpart]'s render, the actual color of his ushanka is brown. However, when used in battle, he is shown to have a red ushanka, similarly to an opponent's Giant Skeleton troop in Clash Royale.
**Unlike his Clash of Clans counterpart, the Giant Skeleton in Clash Royale attacks anything in sight instead of prioritizing buildings.
***Giant Skeleton is also the only 'Giant' card that doesn't target buildings.
**Before the 3/6/2022 maintenance break, the Giant Skeleton's [[Cards|card]] render was taken from his Clash of Clans counterpart's render, except with a color change of his ushanka.
**The bomb and barrel of the Giant Skeleton appear to be taken from a [[w:c:clashofclans:Giant Bomb|Giant Bomb]] from Clash of Clans.
*The Giant Skeleton is one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the [[Archers]], [[Knight]], [[Goblins]], Bomber, Skeletons, [[Barbarians]], Bats, [[Royal Recruits]], Skeleton Barrel, [[Rascals]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Flying Machine]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], Zappies, [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, Skeleton Army, Witch, [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], Balloon, [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], Wall Breakers, [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Mega Knight]], Ram Rider, Miner, Royal Ghost, Ice Wizard, [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], Night Witch, and [[Fisherman]].
*The Giant Skeleton has been featured in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]] outside of the card. More specifically:
**The Giant Skeleton has been featured with multiple [[Buff|buffs]]. More specifically:
***The Giant Skeleton is 1 of 14 troops that has been featured with a [[Buff#Rage|Rage]] buff, the others being [[Electro Spirit]], Giant, Zappies, Guards, Goblin Giant, Electro Dragon, Wall Breakers, [[Electro Giant]], Mega Knight, Ram Rider, [[Electro Wizard]], [[Sparky]], and Royal Ghost.
***The Giant Skeleton is 1 of 2 troops that has been featured with a [[Buff#Death Spawn|Death Spawn]] buff, the other being Balloon.
**The Giant Skeleton is 1 of 10 troops that has been featured under the [[Ruler Ability#Special Delivery|Special Delivery]] [[Ruler Ability|ruler ability]], the others being Knight, Skeleton Barrel, [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], Musketeer, Wizard, P.E.K.K.A, [[Golem]], Sparky, and Royal Ghost.
*The Giant Skeleton has the same walking sound as the Skeleton King.
*He appears to have an underbite, similar to the [[Minions]], Guards, Lava Hound, and [[Super Lava Hound]].
*The Giant Skeleton's ushanka hat is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R504_Kolyma_Highway Road of Bones], a highway in Russia, where up to 1000000 imprisoned laborers died during its construction.
*The Giant Skeleton makes a laughing sound when deployed, possibly a reference to the Clash Royale [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WugvrZBrExY Giant Skeleton commercial].
*The Giant Skeleton is 1 of 15 troops which bring an excited reaction from the audience upon spawning and brings a collective groan from the audience when defeated, as well as a concerning gasp when the opponent plays him, the others include [[Royal Giant]], Giant, P.E.K.K.A., [[Rune Giant]], Goblin Giant, Golem, Bowler, Electro Wizard, Inferno Dragon, Sparky, Lava Hound, Night Witch, Super Lava Hound, and the [[Monk]].
*The Giant Skeleton, along with the Minions, Bomber, Skeletons, Skeleton Dragons, [[Ice Spirit]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Mega Minion]], Ice Golem, Dart Goblin, Elixir Golem, [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], Guards, Baby Dragon, P.E.K.K.A, Golem, Wall Breakers, Bowler, [[Executioner]], Mega Knight, Inferno Dragon, Royal Ghost, Lava Hound, and the Skeleton King are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Monsters monster] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*The Giant Skeleton is unavailable in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]]. More specifically:
**It is 1 of 4 cards that is unavailable in Triple Draft, the others being [[Three Musketeers]], [[Clone]], and [[Mirror]].
*In [[Touchdown]], if a Giant Skeleton is still on the [[Arenas|Arena]] after a touchdown has been scored (unless he scored it himself), will have his dropped bomb cleared.
*The Giant Skeleton is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Giant Skeleton is the subject of 2 [[Emotes]].
**The Giant Skeleton is the subject of a [[King's Tower|Tower Skin]].
**The Giant Skeleton is the subject of a few [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] items.
***The Giant Skeleton is one of the first troops to be the subject of a Battle Banner item, along with the Mini P.E.K.K.A, Dart Goblin, P.E.K.K.A, Prince, Mega Knight, [[Super Witch]], and the [[Golden Knight]].
***The Hole In The Wall frame and the Backpack, Backpack decoration are created by [https://x.com/suzyq53936155 SuzyQ].
***The Harlequin Toad decoration is part of a collaboration with [https://www.playing4theplanet.org/participants/clash-royale Green Game Jam 2023].
*On 1/4/2016, certain Content Creators were given a different version of the game, with a Tombstone that visually looked larger and would spawn Giant Skeletons instead of Skeletons.
*The initial balance change for Giant Skeleton on the [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(3/1/2024)|3/1/2024 balance changes]] was a 8% hitpoints increase, but it was lowered to 6% [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-55-balance-wip last minute].
*Before the Giant Skeleton's card release, the Giant Skeleton's cost was decreased to 6 [[Elixir]] (from 7 Elixir), his hitpoints were decreased by 10%, and his damage was increased by 11%.

